# VAR - Session command variables

```text
VAR
VAR NAME
VAR NAME=value
VAR /D NAME
```

## Enable variables

Variables are off by default. In [CONFIG](CONFIG.HLP), choose F, then C to
select 128, 256 or 512 bytes. Save and cold boot. Ordinary warm boot keeps
active choices. [STAT MEM](STAT.HLP) reports the persistent memory cost.

## Define and substitute

Names are case-insensitive, 1-8 letters, digits or underscores, beginning
with a letter or underscore. Put = immediately after the name. Everything
after it is the value, including spaces, quotes and additional equals signs.
An empty assignment defines an empty value; /D deletes the name.

```text
VAR F=B0:README.TXT
TYPE %F%
```

%NAME% substitutes once; %% produces a literal percent. Inserted text is
not expanded again. Undefined or malformed references and results over 127
characters prevent dispatch and cancel queued work. Failed edits preserve
the old table. There is no program-visible environment API.

## Lifetime and command sources

Values survive ordinary program returns and warm boots. Cold boot resets
them; STARTUP or [SUBMIT](SUBMIT.HLP) can define them again.
[MCL](MCL.HLP) splits interactive commands before substitution, so inserted
semicolons cannot create new commands. Startup/submitted commands expand
individually; program input, including XSUB input, remains literal.
